THIRD-PARTY MODELS
================================================================================

IndicTrans2 (ai4bharat/indictrans2-en-indic-1B,
             ai4bharat/indictrans2-en-indic-dist-200M,
             ai4bharat/indictrans2-indic-en-1B)
AI4Bharat, IIT Madras — MIT License
https://github.com/ai4bharat/IndicTrans2/blob/main/LICENSE

  Base checkpoints fine-tuned by this project. MIT permits redistribution of
  derivative weights under Apache-2.0 provided the MIT notice is retained.

IndicTransToolkit
AI4Bharat, IIT Madras — MIT License
  Provides IndicProcessor, required for IndicTrans2 pre/post-processing.

LaBSE (sentence-transformers/LaBSE)
Google / sentence-transformers — Apache-2.0

  Used only for parallel-corpus quality filtering. Does not contribute to
  released model weights.

KashmiriNormalizer (pinned ==0.1.0)
  The official KATHE 2026 scorer's normalizer, used for evaluation and for
  normalizing training targets.

================================================================================
NOT USED IN RELEASED ARTIFACTS
================================================================================

facebook/nllb-200-distilled-1.3B is CC-BY-NC-4.0 (non-commercial).

  The KATHE 2026 organizers ruled on 2026-08-08 that any open-source model may
  be used "even if it is not allowed to commercially use licences like GPL",
  so this licence is not a bar to entry. NLLB is nonetheless not used by this
  project, on cost grounds: a second full fine-tune is a large share of the
  available GPU budget for uncertain gain.

  No NLLB-derived weights are included in any artifact released here. If that
  changes, the derived weights must be published under NLLB's own licence
  rather than Apache-2.0 — a non-commercial term cannot be relicensed away —
  and both this notice and MODEL_CARD.md must be updated to say so.
